@startuml
title Slurm + Dask Deployment (single sbatch allocation)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Slurm Allocation\n(examples/hpc/slurm/train_dask.sbatch)" {
  node "Batch step (node 0)" as Batch {
    component "Driver process\n(examples/hpc/train_ea_dask.py\nor any make_executor caller)" as Driver
  }

  node "srun --overlap step 1\n(node 0)" as SchedStep {
    component "dask scheduler\n--scheduler-file $SCHED_FILE" as Scheduler
  }

  node "srun --overlap step 2\n(--ntasks=$SLURM_JOB_NUM_NODES)" {
    node "Worker task (node 0)" as WNode0 {
      component "dask worker(s)\n--nthreads 1\n--nworkers $SLURM_CPUS_PER_TASK" as W0
    }
    node "Worker task (node 1..N)" as WNodeN {
      component "dask worker(s)\n--nthreads 1\n--nworkers $SLURM_CPUS_PER_TASK" as WN
    }
  }
}

database "Shared filesystem\n($SHARED_DIR)" as FS {
  artifact "$SCHED_FILE\n(scheduler connection info)" as SchedFile
  artifact "TrainingConfig.output_dir\n(metrics.csv, summary.json)" as Results
}

actor "Cluster scheduler\n(slurmctld / slurmd)" as Slurm

Slurm -> Batch : allocates nodes,\nlaunches sbatch script
Batch -> SchedStep : srun --overlap\n(shares allocation's CPUs)
Batch -> WNode0 : srun --overlap\n(shares allocation's CPUs)
Batch -> WNodeN : srun --overlap\n(shares allocation's CPUs)

Scheduler -> SchedFile : writes address/ports\non bind
Driver -> SchedFile : polls for file\n(up to 60s), then reads
Driver ..> Scheduler : DEAP_DASK_SCHEDULER=$SCHED_FILE\n-> make_executor resolves via\nresolve_scheduler_address\n-> Client(scheduler_file=...)

W0 --> SchedFile : reads to locate scheduler
WN --> SchedFile : reads to locate scheduler
W0 ..> Scheduler : registers as worker
WN ..> Scheduler : registers as worker

Driver -> Scheduler : client.map(_worker_evaluate, payloads)\n(dispatch via registered workers)
Scheduler --> W0 : task
Scheduler --> WN : task
W0 --> Scheduler : (fitness, steps_delta)
WN --> Scheduler : (fitness, steps_delta)
Scheduler --> Driver : gathered results\n(ordered; retries=2 on worker death)

Driver -> Results : write metrics.csv,\nsummary.json, checkpoint\n(single writer -- ExperimentLogger)

note bottom of Driver
  Real-cluster deltas vs the Docker Slurm rig
  (docker/slurm-cluster/, tests/hpc/test_slurm_rig.py)
  are only partition/account sbatch headers and
  node counts -- the same .sbatch file is submitted
  in both places.
end note

note bottom of FS
  Scheduler-file handshake is the canonical
  dask-on-Slurm pattern: the scheduler's
  hostname/port are not known ahead of the
  allocation, so workers and the driver discover
  them via a shared-FS file instead of a fixed
  tcp:// address (used by the Docker Dask rig,
  docker/dask-cluster/, instead).
end note
@enduml
